### Reservation System Test

### 1. Login to get token
POST http://localhost:3031/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "marco@italiandelight.com",
  "password": "Password123",
  "businessId": 1
}

### 2. Get all tables (should show reservation data for reserved tables)
GET http://localhost:3031/api/tables
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 3. Get specific table with reservation
GET http://localhost:3031/api/tables/3
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 4. Get floor plan with tables (should show reservation data)
GET http://localhost:3031/api/floor-plans/1/tables
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 5. Get all reservations
GET http://localhost:3031/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 6. Get specific reservation
GET http://localhost:3031/api/reservations/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 7. Create new reservation
POST http://localhost:3031/api/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tableId": 4,
  "customerName": "Test Customer",
  "customerPhone": "+1-555-9999",
  "customerEmail": "test@example.com",
  "partySize": 3,
  "reservationDate": "2025-01-15",
  "reservationTime": "19:30:00",
  "status": "pending",
  "specialRequests": "Test reservation"
}

### 8. Update reservation
PUT http://localhost:3031/api/reservations/1
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "confirmed",
  "specialRequests": "Updated special requests"
}

### 9. Delete reservation
DELETE http://localhost:3031/api/reservations/4
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### 10. Test tables after reservation creation (should show new reservation)
GET http://localhost:3031/api/tables
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}} 